  "scope": "All-mode mapped connectivity and retained Liberty area. Bit planes keep both atomic banks; word/read-tree tiles keep all data bits of consecutive/equal-low-bit entries within one bank. Data-bearing gates follow their map support; zero-map-support gates join a slice only when every consumer is local. Remaining shared support is counted once. Clock/constants excluded from net budgets; reset included. These are graph cuts, not placement, wire length, timing or an optimal partition.",
  "limitations": [
    "Conservative all-mode dependencies are not timing paths or an independent behavioral proof.",
    "Area is retained Liberty cell area; shared support is counted once. No whitespace, new buffering or routing area is predicted.",
    "Graph-cut net counts do not rank actual routed cost; five large planes and 32 small tiles are different granularities.",
    "The proposed 18 functional input bits and 10 output bits are a future module contract, not a measured reduction from 280 mapped incoming nets.",
    "No new synthesis, RTL simulation, OpenDB export, placement or routing in this increment. Existing macro/full-package proof boundaries and licensing remain open."
  ]
